[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/d3Ex22/TCGCardShopSimulator-Mods/main/SmartWorkerRestock/NexusMods/header_1400x400.jpg[/img]

[size=5][b][color=#E0B13A]Your workers order what your shelves need, finish opened boxes first and refill the emptiest shelves first.[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#C9C9C9]Built for the latest game version and made to sit alongside other worker mods.[/color][/size]

[url=https://github.com/d3Ex22/TCGCardShopSimulator-Mods/tree/main/SmartWorkerRestock][img]https://img.shields.io/badge/source-GitHub-181717?style=for-the-badge&logo=github&logoColor=white[/img][/url] [img]https://img.shields.io/badge/version-1.5.0-B3402E?style=for-the-badge[/img] [img]https://img.shields.io/badge/BepInEx-5.4.23-3E7B3A?style=for-the-badge[/img] [img]https://img.shields.io/badge/AI--made-Claude-E0B13A?style=for-the-badge[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#E0B13A]Description[/color][/b][/size]

[size=3]Hired workers can restock your shop, but someone still has to order the stock, half-used boxes pile up in the warehouse while new ones get opened, and the shelf they refill is picked at random. Smart Worker Restock takes care of that:

[list]
[*][b]Automatic orders[/b] that buy only what your shelves need, counting the stock you already have.
[*][b]Opened boxes first[/b]: workers finish half-used boxes before opening new ones.
[*][b]Emptiest shelves first[/b]: workers refill what is running out before what is almost full.
[/list][/size]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/d3Ex22/TCGCardShopSimulator-Mods/main/SmartWorkerRestock/NexusMods/main_1920x1080.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#E0B13A]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#E9DCB5]Automatic orders[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3]Every 45 seconds, the mod looks at every shop compartment filled at 80 % or less, subtracts what you already have (boxes stored in the warehouse, boxes lying around, boxes on their way) and orders the difference in whole boxes, emptiest shelves first.
[list]
[*]Your [b]money reserve[/b] is never touched, 500 by default.
[*]Only items whose [b]license you bought[/b] are ordered.
[*]Paid and booked like the game's own restock checkout: delivery fee, transactions, daily report and shop experience.
[*]An item is not ordered again for 3 minutes, so boxes still on their way are [b]never ordered twice[/b].
[/list][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#E9DCB5]Opened boxes first[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3]When a worker is about to open a full box, he takes the [b]emptiest opened box[/b] of the same item and size instead, on the floor or on a warehouse shelf. A box another worker is already going for is left alone.[/size]

[size=4][b][color=#E9DCB5]Emptiest shelves first[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3]The game picks the item to restock and the compartment to fill at random. With Smart Worker Restock, a worker restocks the item whose compartment is the [b]emptiest[/b], then fills the emptiest compartment of what he carries, the nearest one on a tie. Workers going for the same item spread over its compartments. [i]RestockPriority[/i] sets what "emptiest" means: fewest items, lowest fill, or the game's random choice.[/size]

[size=4][b][color=#E9DCB5]Worker AI Overhaul[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3]Worker AI Overhaul also decides which box and shelf your workers go for. When it is installed, a window lets you choose once a save is loaded:
[list]
[*][b]Compatibility mode[/b]: Worker AI Overhaul makes those choices and Smart Worker Restock only orders stock.
[*][b]Keep Smart Worker Restock's choices[/b]: opened boxes first and emptiest shelves first apply as usual.
[/list]
You can change it later with [i]WorkerAIOverhaulMode[/i].[/size]

[spoiler][size=3][b]Settings[/b]: [i]BepInEx/config/gab.tcgshop.smartworkerrestock.cfg[/i], also available in game through the Configuration Manager.
[list]
[*][b]Enabled[/b] (true): turns the whole mod on or off.
[*][b]RequireHiredWorker[/b] (true): only order while a worker is on the clock.
[*][b]CheckIntervalSeconds[/b] (45): time between two stock checks.
[*][b]OrderBelowFillPercent[/b] (80 %): a compartment needs stock at or below this fill.
[*][b]ExtraBoxesInReserve[/b] (0): extra boxes to keep for each item that needs stock.
[*][b]MoneyReserve[/b] (500): money automatic orders never spend.
[*][b]MaxItemTypesPerOrder[/b] (20): different items in one order.
[*][b]ReorderCooldownSeconds[/b] (180): wait before ordering the same item again.
[*][b]PreferBigBox[/b] (true): order big boxes when both sizes are unlocked.
[*][b]UseOpenedBoxesFirst[/b] (true): opened boxes before full ones.
[*][b]RestockPriority[/b] (LowestCount): LowestCount, LowestFillPercent or GameDefault.
[*][b]WorkerAIOverhaulMode[/b] (Ask): Ask, Compatibility or Override.
[/list]
Every order and every opened box taken instead of a full one is written to the BepInEx log.[/size][/spoiler]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#E0B13A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[size=3][list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases]BepInEx 5.4.23[/url].
[*]Remove [b]Auto Worker Order[/b] if you have it: Smart Worker Restock replaces it and stays idle while it is installed.
[*]Install with your mod manager, or extract the archive into the game folder to get [i]BepInEx/plugins/SmartWorkerRestock/SmartWorkerRestock.dll[/i].
[/list][/size]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#E0B13A]Requirements and compatibility[/color][/b][/size]

[size=3][list]
[*][b]TCG Card Shop Simulator[/b], latest version, and [url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases]BepInEx 5.4.23[/url].
[*]At least one hired worker, or turn [i]RequireHiredWorker[/i] off.
[*]Works alongside Staff Overhaul, QOL Events & Weather, Pallet Delivery and other worker mods.
[*]With [b]Worker AI Overhaul[/b], you choose which mod handles the workers' choices, see above.
[*]Replaces [b]Auto Worker Order[/b]: do not use both.
[/list][/size]

[line]

